  "worked_solution": "Recall the following special limit: \n\n$$\n{e}^{x}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{-6n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{[{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{n}]}^{-6} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{n}]}^{-6} \\\\  & ={({e}^{x})}^{-6} \\\\  & ={e}^{-6x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{6x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
